-- title:
--   Equivariant Čerednik–Drinfeld family of fine moduli points
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r\neq r$ (`hrr`) and $N$ is a nonzero squarefree integer divisible by neither (`hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Local base data.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic-zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi$ an irreducible element (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), $\#(\mathcal O/(\pi))=r$ (`hres`) and $(r)=(\pi)$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (written `Onr`) is a characteristic-zero domain and an $\mathcal O$-algebra, with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, such that $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is $(\pi)$-adically complete (`hOnr_complete`), $(\pi)O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element satisfies some monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ has a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x)\equiv x^{r}\pmod{\pi}$ (`hFr`). Finally $v_{\det}\colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)\to\mathbb Z$ is a homomorphism with $v_{\det}(g)=n$ if and only if $\det g=u\pi^{n}$ for some $u\in\mathcal O^{\times}$ (`hvdet`).
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli data.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ satisfies `IsIndefiniteRamifiedExactlyAt a b r rbar`: $0<a$ or $0<b$, and a finite place of $\mathbb Q$ is ramified exactly when it lies over $r$ or $\bar r$ (`hB`); $\Lambda$ is a maximal order (`hΛ`). The scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `pt` is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure (`h𝒳`, the five clauses of `IsCoarseModuli`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with base change, bijectivity on geometric points, and the universal property). The integer $n$ satisfies $3\le n$, $r\nmid n$, $\bar r\nmid n$, $\gcd(n,N)=1$; $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptF` is a fine moduli space for pairs $(E,P)$ with $P$ a full level-$n$ structure (`hM`, the four clauses of `IsFineModuli`), and $G$ is a group acting on $M$ through $\rho\colon G\to\operatorname{Aut}M$ with labels $\chi\colon G\to\Lambda$ forming a level-twist action (`hρ`: the action is over the base and realises the twists `WithFullLevel.IsTwist` by $\chi(g)$, together with the multiplicativity, surjectivity and injectivity clauses for $\chi$ modulo $n$). The forgetful morphism $p\colon M\to\mathcal X$ lies over the base (`hp`), is $\rho$-invariant (`hρp`) and sends the fine point of $(E,P)$ to the coarse point of $E$ (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke and Atkin–Lehner data.** For each prime $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ a scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map `ptT ℓ` is a coarse moduli space for curves with an extra level-$\ell$ subgroup (`h𝒴`), and $d_0,d_1\colon\mathcal Y_\ell\to\mathcal X$ lie over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`) and compute, on points, the source of the extra level structure (`hd₀`) and its $\ell$-isogenous quotient (`hd₁`). Endomorphisms $a_r,a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ lie over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) and realise on points the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side and uniformising group.** $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); $n_1$ is a finite idele in `primeHeckeSet R₁ r` (`hn₁`) with `meetOrder R₁ n₁` Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]\to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); $v$ is a height-one prime containing $r$ (`hv`). The subgroup $\Gamma^{t}$ is the group `awayUnits R₁ v` of units integral away from $v$ (`hΓt`); for each $\ell\notin\{r,\bar r\}$ elements $s_\ell$ and $sf_\ell$ are given whose local components away from $r$ are $s_\ell\otimes 1$ and whose component at $r$ is $1$, such that the diagonal idele of $\ell$ times $sf_\ell^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell\mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell)=\ell$ (`hs`); $\Gamma^{t}_\ell=\Gamma^{t}\cap s_\ell\Gamma^{t}s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`); and $\bar w$ has reduced norm $\bar r$ and normalises $\Gamma^{t}$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Special-fibre data.** $\Lambda$ contains the rational integers (`hΛℤ`) and `coord` is an order coordinate for $\Lambda$ at $r$ (`hcoord`, the clauses of `IsOrderCoord`: additivity, normalisation, the Witt-vector multiplication rule, injectivity, density and the trace rule). Over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ there are a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ for $A_0$, and `hA₀` asserting that $A_0$ is a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$. Families $e,e'\colon\Gamma^{t}\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`he`) with degrees `deg` satisfy: `hE1`, each $(e\gamma,e'\gamma)$ is a level-preserving isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$; `hE1mul`, multiplicativity up to powers of $r$; `hE1sc`, rational scalars act as such up to powers of $r$; `hE1'`, conversely an $e\gamma$ that is a scalar up to powers of $r$ forces $\gamma$ to be a rational scalar; `hE2`, for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by an element of that centraliser whose $E_0$-image is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$; `hE3`, labelling of the action of $\Gamma^{t}$ on full level-$n$ structures by $\Lambda$ modulo $n$; `hE4`, over algebraically closed fields every level-preserving $r$-power isogeny self-pair of a pullback of $A_0$ comes from some $\gamma\in\Gamma^{t}$. An order $R_2\le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power dense image in $R_1$ (`hR₂r`) carries $\hat e\colon R_2\to\operatorname{End}(A_0)$ over the base (`hê`) subject to `hE5a` (additivity, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action, preservation of level), `hE5b1`–`hE5b3` (unit, multiplicativity, integers), `hE5c` (the conjugate composes to multiplication by the reduced norm), `hE5d` (compatibility with $e$ on $r$-power multiples of elements of $\Gamma^{t}$) and `hE5e` (a single $g$ linearising both $e$ on $\Gamma^{t}$ and $\hat e$ on $R_2$ as above).
--
--   **Drinfeld-module side.** $\iota\colon \mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, $\Phi$ a special formal module of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), `MD` a moduli package which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ a map from rigidified objects to `MD` satisfying the three clauses `hη`: on admissible objects over Noetherian rings $\eta$ identifies exactly the isomorphic ones, $\eta$ is natural in the base, and every element of `MD.obj` is, over a finite localisation cover generating the unit ideal, the $\eta$-image of an admissible object. $E_0$ is an injective ring map from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is squeezed between $r^{m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ and $r^{-m}M_2(\mathcal O)$ for some $m$ (`hE₀`). A family $eD$ is given, from the functor of $G$-points of `MD` over $\mathcal O$ to the product of the functor $B\mapsto(O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)$ with Deligne's functor $\Omega$ of lines in lattice base changes, which is natural (`hnatD`), bijective on every Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent $\mathcal O$-algebra (`hbijD`), has first component the structural map $\psi$ (`hfstD`), converts the action `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy ι Φ η Fr E₀ g` into the twisted action `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B g` (`hGLD`), and converts $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist of the first component with unchanged second component (`hPiD`), $\pi$-translates existing always (`hPiexD`). Further, $\kappa\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)\to O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ is compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`) and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to $X_0\otimes_\kappa$ of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A base full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ is fixed.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner partner of $A_0$.** A second curve $A_0^{w}$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ with morphisms $a_w,a_w',b_w,b_w'$ over the base (`haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`) realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ (`hBSw`) preserving level (`hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw` provides a single $g\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ linearising simultaneously the $e\gamma$ as $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$ and the composite $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ as $r^{k_w}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The point map $\Xi$ and the comparison hypotheses.** $\Xi$ assigns to every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, every $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B$ and every rigidified curve $(E,\varrho)$ over $B$ a $G$-point of `MD`, subject to: `hΞleg`, over connected $B$ the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-component of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist of $\psi$; `hΞnat`, naturality under pullbacks of rigidified curves; `hΞiso`, invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves matching the rigidifications up to $r$-power comparison; `hΞdef`, an explicit description of $\Xi$ through $\eta$, by means of a rigidification transport with exponent $j\le 1$ producing an admissible rigidified object whose formal module is the given one. Finally $g_0\in\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed, and: `heqΓ`, over connected $B$ a translation of rigidifications by $e\gamma$ is converted by $\Xi$ into the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$ for some $c\in\mathbb Z$; `heqW`, when $\bar r$ is invertible in $B$ the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$, matched with $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ on rigidifications, is converted into the action of $r^{c}\,g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$. The four clauses `hK1`–`hK4` provide, for the twist $\psi^{\ast}=\mathrm{frobTwist}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}\,\mathrm{Fr}\,(-v_{\det}(g_0))\,\psi$: existence over connected $B$ of a rigidified pair whose $\Xi$-image has leg $\psi^{\ast}$ and is carried by the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action onto $(\psi,P)$ (`hK1`); uniqueness of such a pair up to an isomorphism compatible with the rigidifications (`hK2`); its base change along $\mathcal O$-algebra maps (`hK3`); and its lifting along a surjection $p\colon B\to B_0$ whose kernel squares to zero in the stated sense (`hK4`). The clauses `hC0e` and `hC0u` give, for a rigidified pair over connected $B$ together with a formal module structure on $E$, the existence of a full level-$n$ structure which is the height-normalised transport `IsNormLevelTransport` of $P_0$ along $\varrho$, and the uniqueness of its underlying section.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses there exists a family
--   $$\Theta^{c}_B\colon \bigl((O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega(B)\bigr)\times G\longrightarrow \{\varphi\colon \operatorname{Spec}B\to M \mid \varphi\ \text{followed by}\ f_M\ \text{is the structural map}\},$$
--   defined for every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, with the following four properties.
--
--   First, $\Theta^{c}$ is natural: for all such $B,B'$ and every $\mathcal O$-algebra map $\varphi\colon B\to B'$, $\Theta^{c}_{B'}$ of the transport of $x$ along $\varphi$ equals the transport along $\varphi$ of $\Theta^{c}_B(x)$ in `Scheme.nilpPoints fM`.
--
--   Second, $\Theta^{c}$ is $G$-equivariant in the sense that for all $x\in (O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B)\times\Omega(B)$ and all $g,h\in G$, the morphism $\Theta^{c}_B(x,gh)$ followed by $\rho(h)$ equals $\Theta^{c}_B(x,g)$.
--
--   Third, the value of $\Theta^{c}$ is pinned on rigidified pairs: for every $\psi\colon O^{\mathrm{nr}}\to_{\mathcal O}B$, every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, every $g\in G$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$, every rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along $\psi^{\ast}=\mathrm{frobTwist}\,O^{\mathrm{nr}}\,\mathrm{Fr}\,(-v_{\det}(g_0))\,\psi$, and every full level-$n$ structure $P_n$ on $E$, if the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-leg of $\Xi_B(\psi^{\ast})(E,\varrho)$ is $\psi^{\ast}$, if $eD$ carries that $G$-point to $(\psi,P)$ under the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted action (so that $\psi$ is the prescribed Frobenius twist of the leg and $P$ is the pullback of the associated Deligne datum along $g_0$), and if $P_n$ is a height-normalised level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho$, then the underlying morphism of $\Theta^{c}_B((\psi,P),g)$ equals the fine-moduli point $\mathrm{ptF}_B(E,P_n)$ followed by $\rho(g^{-1})$.
--
--   Fourth, under the same hypotheses on $B,\psi,P,g,E,\varrho$ (no level structure being required), the underlying morphism of $\Theta^{c}_B((\psi,P),g)$ followed by $p$ equals the coarse-moduli point $\mathrm{pt}_B(E)$.
--
--   This is the construction step of the Čerednik–Drinfeld $p$-adic uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: it produces, over Noetherian $\pi$-nilpotent connected bases, a $G$-equivariant family of points of the fine moduli scheme $M$ whose value is prescribed on every rigidified pair coming from Drinfeld's formal upper half plane, compatibly with the forgetful map to the coarse moduli space $\mathcal X$. It is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_conn`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.IsFineModuli.exists_fineFamily_of_evenRigidifiedPair_of_isNoetherianRing_heightNormalised_conn), where the extension, equivariance and lifting steps are carried out for any family with this prescribed value.
